WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.250
Justine - Hey guys it's Justine and
today we're checking out

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.360
these brand new headphones by Dolby.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.360
These are the Dolby Dimension headphones.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.710
These feature a few new things

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.300
that I'm really excited to test out,

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.720
most of which, there's
this thing called LifeMix.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.930
You can put the headphones
on and you can decide

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.070
how much of the outside
noise you wanna hear

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.840
and how much of your
content you wanna hear.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.580
That's gonna be really fun,
because my sister and I

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.290
do edit a lot side by side.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.210
She'll be editing a video,

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.580
I don't wanna actually hear her video,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.610
but she wants to be able
to hear me talking to her

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.530
and vice versa.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:28.380
I'm also excited about the Cinematic Sound

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.580
when you move your head,
you'll be able to hear

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.680
the change in whatever it
is that you're watching

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.370
so it's really like you are so immersed

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:36.190
that you're actually there.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:37.160
A huge thank you to Dolby

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.520
for partnering with me on this video.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.210
When they reached out
about these headphones

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.710
I was so excited, because
I'm such a huge fan of Dolby.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.150
When you hear the name
Dolby, you automatically know

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.160
that it's going to be
something that is incredible

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.890
because they've been around for so long

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.730
and it's one of those
names that you just trust.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:55.928
So I just knew that this is
something that I had to try out.

00:00:55.928 --> 00:00:58.251
(light electronic music)

00:00:58.251 --> 00:00:59.330
Look at these.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.070
They're on like a little pillow.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.580
These headphones look so comfortable,

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.820
makes me wanna take a nap.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.290
So, nice weight,

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.630
a really,

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.850
really nice feel.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.070
They fit me perfectly, I
didn't have to adjust anything.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.450
Am I yelling? I might be yelling.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.680
Anytime I put headphones on
I automatically start yelling

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.250
because I can't really hear myself.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.600
It's got a little L
and the R inside there.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.710
This is so comfortable,

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.560
it has like a nice padding up at the top

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.730
and this is like a perfect
fit over top of your ears.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.370
Sometimes I feel like
these types of headphones

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:26.810
can be a little bit overpowering,

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.820
but they sit just perfectly,
they're extremely comfortable.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.340
I wish that I could put
these on your little head.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.685
Here, let's try them.

00:01:34.685 --> 00:01:35.820
(electronic music)

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.110
Well how does that feel?

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.343
I wish that you could experience it.

00:01:38.343 --> 00:01:40.200
It's the hardest part
when I'm making videos

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.880
it's how do I accurately
describe what I'm feeling,

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.320
and I try really hard.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.600
I'm sometimes not good
ad describing my feelings

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.990
but I'm feeling pretty
excited about these.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.700
Let's see what else is inside here.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.460
I think that Dolby should also
consider making bed sheets

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.470
because this is something

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:56.880
that I would like to take a nap in.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.700
You guys get in there.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.920
Well that is so soft.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.150
So what I think it's
really cool about these

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:03.300
is you can pair three
separate devices to it

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.200
at the same time, and you
can switch between them.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.780
So a lot of times I'll be on my phone,

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.370
I'll be on my iMac and
I'll be on my laptop

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.400
especially when I'm traveling

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.780
I want to switch between
my music or my editing,

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.880
and really, it's just
great to be able to have

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.750
this one press of a
button to switch between

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.000
all of the things that are connected.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.170
This also acts as touch
control, so if you tap twice,

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.670
you can toggle between LifeMix
and active noise cancellation

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:26.930
and there's an accompanying
app that goes with this

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.440
so you're able to control
just how that mix sounds.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.270
And you can control your headphones.

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:34.180
So there's Virtualization
and Head Tracking.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:35.930
This is where you can pair
each one of your devices,

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.610
that corresponds to each of the buttons

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:38.910
that you have on the headset,

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.110
so if I wanna connect my
phone, it's the first one

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:42.850
and when I connect my laptop and iMac,

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:43.970
those will be the next two.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.850
So I guess now that I have this set up,

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.520
I need to play something.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.710
Let's listen to the new
Imagine Dragons album.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:51.543
(electronic music)
- I wish

00:02:51.543 --> 00:02:54.320
so you could experience this.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.020
Okay, I wanna check out the LifeMix.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:00.033
So to do that I gotta tap twice to toggle.

00:03:00.982 --> 00:03:03.090
(volume of music decreases)

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:03.923
Hello?

00:03:03.923 --> 00:03:05.120
Oh my God! This is so weird.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.310
What, is ha--

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.970
Woo!

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.030
Oh my God.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.610
This is so silly.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:12.270
I do tend to overreact a lot

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.310
but this is unlike anything that

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:18.070
I feel like I've really
experienced in headphones before.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.970
So when I double tap,

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.330
right now

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.070
I can't hear myself even talking.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.030
All I hear is the music.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.620
I double tap, that activates the LifeMix,

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.730
so it's like microphones
are now picking up

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:31.940
what is around me.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.290
Like, I can hear myself
inside of my head playing

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.290
while my music is playing.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.070
That's the only way that I can explain it.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.120
This is

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.720
so

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:41.770
wild.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:43.080
So if you've ever had headphones on

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.150
while you're recording something

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:45.530
and the only way that I
can kind of explain it

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:46.860
is you put the headphones on

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.690
you can also monitor yourself talking

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.210
it's picking up my voice.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.670
Oh my gosh I can't wait to try this.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.310
I can't wait to get Jenna's reaction

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.660
she has no idea.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.080
Like, I read about what this feature was.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:57.990
This is not.

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:00.010
There's also a little charging dock.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:00.920
So I'm gonna try and give you guys

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.620
an audio example of what I'm hearing.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.810
Picture right now that you
have the headphones on.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.310
And this is what it sounds like

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.224
if I was talking to you right now.

00:04:08.224 --> 00:04:09.080
(volume of music increases)
So you can't really hear me,

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.920
it's muffled, it's, you know, like

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:13.270
Justine I can sort of hear you

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.330
but I'm listening to music
and I can't hear you.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.670
Now when I turn these on

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:19.280
with that LifeMix

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.490
this is what it sounds like.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:23.080
So it's kind of like,
everything is at a perfect mix

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.010
my voice is recorded into the song

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.610
so everything is just,

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.811
it's called LifeMix for a reason.

00:04:28.811 --> 00:04:29.770
What?!

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.200
I need to go watch some content

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.880
I need to connect the rest of my devices

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.150
there's so many things
that I wanna do now.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.280
I need a moment.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.113
Jenna!

00:04:37.113 --> 00:04:39.130
Dude, these are so freackin' cool.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.130
You're gonna see, you're gonna see soon.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:42.783
You're gonna see so, so soon.

